      "title": "file: Remove unnecessary priming of tap fields",
      "message": "file: Remove unnecessary priming of tap fields\n\nCommit 0f3f207967a99f2d101f80d1d878d33e30c1b52e made it so the\nLua dfilter (used by field extractors) always primes the tree in\nepan_dissect_run. This was aimed at solving #6020, but also solved\nissue #4058. (See also commit e162470d6b60999deebdb389cdba33e6ddd97ca5.)\n\nPriming only the Lua fields is a cleaner way to assure that the\nLua ProtoField can extract its desired fields, without priming\nthe tree with fields from the other (more normal) taps when we're\nnot running the taps.\n\nRemove the call to tap_build_interesting in cf_select_packet because\nit's not needed and only slows down dissection a bit.\n",
